      "raw_answer": "The change is a pure deletion of the `/admin/audit` endpoint, which was properly gated with `@require_role(\"admin\")` in the base. Removing an admin-only endpoint does not introduce a new authorization flaw \u2014 it only reduces the attack surface. The remaining `/admin/stats` endpoint still enforces `@require_role(\"admin\")` and only exposes aggregate counts (no user-controlled identifier, no ownership check needed). No new access path is created, and no previously protected operation is left unauthenticated.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"findings\": []\n}\n```",
